llm.completionCheck:
[Completion check] You just stopped. Check your work against the user's original request once (do not redo it from scratch):
{list}{cut}
Then do exactly one of these:
1. Everything the user asked for is done ⇒ reply only NO_REPLY (nothing else);
2. It is done but the plan status was not updated ⇒ mark it with plan_verify and real evidence, then reply NO_REPLY;
3. Something really is still missing ⇒ do only the missing part (do not regenerate or reopen files that were already created or opened), then report briefly.

llm.continueLongTextFile:
[Keep writing · not long enough yet] The user asked for {n} characters and that is **not reached yet** (the counts below are measured by the host; saying it is enough does not make it enough). Text files written in this task:
{files}
The long text is in "{file}", currently {x} characters. **Append the next part to the end of this file**: call write_file with path exactly "{file}" and append:true (do not rewrite the opening, do not overwrite, do not create another file), part by part until the length requirement is met; do not redo steps that are already done. After each write the host appends a [Length progress] line to the tool result (counted without whitespace); use it to decide whether to keep writing.

llm.continueLongTextNew:
[Keep writing · the long text has not started] The user asked for a long text of at least {n} characters, but none of the files written in this task is that long text:
{files}
Use write_file to **create a new file** with the first part (do not write into the files above), then keep appending to that new file with append:true until the length requirement is met.

llm.stepAlreadyDone:
[Done · not redone] {why} (already done at {time}); the host did not run it again.
Previous result: {result}
Go straight to what is not done yet; once everything is done, report the result to the user in text.

llm.writeOverwriteBlocked:
[Not written] {path} already holds {old} chars written earlier in this task; this content ({new} chars) {why}, so overwriting would lose what is already written. The host did not perform this write.
· To continue writing: send this content again unchanged with append:true (appends to the end of the file);
· To change part of it: use edit_file;
· To really replace the whole file with this content: send it again with overwrite:true.
